> 0 be such that ωp+θ > 0. The existence is proved using the contraction mapping principle in the space\n\nE := {U ∈ C([0,∞),Xp) : U E = sup t≥0\n\ne−(ω\n\np+θ)t U(t) p < ∞} ,\n\nthat is a Banach space when endowed with the norm U E. Hence, given U ∈ E, we set\n\nt\n\nΦ(U)(t) = etAUin +\n\ne(t−s)AFM(U(s))ds , ∀t ≥ 0 .\n\n0\n\n35\n\n",
